## 4. Handoff to product and technical review

KB checks cover knowledge material and its use. PC01–PC15 and TC01–TC15 retain
their product and technical document scopes. Report the three outcomes in
parallel and connect object, source, requirement, issue and acceptance IDs.
Use the provenance for the original PC and TC references. Determine each
rule's outcome from its own evidence.

| Knowledge finding | Related product checks | Related technical checks | Handoff |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Source, adoption, version, or baseline gap | PC04, PC15 | TC01, TC14, TC15 | Provide original text, locator, scope, and gap. Assess the related rule independently. |
| Isolation, transfer, deletion, or recovery gap | PC09, PC10, PC14 | TC04, TC05, TC06, TC09 | Link features, states, interfaces, permissions, and tasks. Retain L3 gaps for unverified behavior. |
| Insufficient retrieval, source change, or conflict | PC03, PC04, PC13, PC15 | TC02, TC07, TC14, TC15 | Update issues and dependencies. Await real user tradeoffs and recheck affected conclusions. |
| Evidence or acceptance counting gap | PC12, PC15 | TC12, TC13, TC15 | Complete acceptance design and evidence plans. Record actual passes and technical feasibility closure separately. |

Retain the KB rule or issue, source version or excerpt, SOP section or
requirement, PC/TC rule or issue, task or acceptance condition, and required
level, blocker, and confirmation. Verify each check against its own conditions.
